# Equinox counts only the lands Cleansing's destruction could destroy (CR 702.12b; the owner's rule for Cleansing): Bot1
# controls two Plains and Darksteel Citadel, indestructible, and each player has 1 life. Two destructible lands are no
# more than the 2 life the players could pay, so sparing both is a choice they may make, and Cleansing is not countered
# (rulings: not if it destroys a land only if a choice is made). Bot2's own Islands are not Bot1's and count for nothing.
# Then no one pays: the Plains and Islands are destroyed, the Citadel stays.

[Life]
Bot1: 1
Bot2: 1

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Equinox
Darksteel Citadel
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Cleansing
Island
Island x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Equinox.Cast(Plains)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Darksteel Citadel.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Hand.Cleansing.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate(Stack.Cleansing; Ability: Counter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield = Darksteel Citadel; Equinox; Mox Pearl; Plains; Plains
Bot2.Choose()
Bot1.Choose()

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Darksteel Citadel; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Life = 1
Bot2.Life = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
